  "question": {
    "text": "Length, breadth and thickness of a strip having a uniform cross section are measured to be 10.5 cm , 0.05 mm , and $6.0 \\mu \\mathrm{~m}$, respectively. Which of the following option(s) give(s) the volume of the strip in $\\mathrm{cm}^3$ with correct significant figures:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Y9lxp",
      "text": "$3.2 \\times 10^{-5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IIIwX",
      "text": "$32.0 \\times 10^{-6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vvixE",
      "text": "$3.0 \\times 10^{-5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hxWR1",
      "text": "$3 \\times 10^{-5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{L}=10.5 \\mathrm{~cm} \\rightarrow 3$ significant digits\n$\\mathrm{b}=0.05 \\mathrm{~cm} \\rightarrow 1$ significant digit\n$\\mathrm{t}=6.0 \\mu \\mathrm{~m} \\rightarrow 2$ significant digits\nVolume, $\\mathrm{V}=$ Lbt must have only 1 significant digit\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{V}=10.5 \\times 0.05 \\times 10^{-1} \\times 6.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~cm}^3 \\\\\n& =3 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{cc}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
